    "checks": [
      "An in-law suite is a residential accessory use allowed by right (zoning permit) in R-1, R-2, R-3, R-4 and R-5, on a lot with a single-family detached house (143-32, 143-36, 143-48, 143-52, 143-56, 143-6.2)",
      "It must be inside the house or inside a detached household garage on the same lot (143-6.2, in-law suite)",
      "Family only: at most two members of the family living in the house. The owner files a statement by January 15 each year, and removes the separate kitchen when those people no longer live there (143-6.2, in-law suite (6) to (11))",
      "Size: the suite may not exceed 50% of the house's 'primary living area' (living room, dining room, kitchen, one bathroom and the largest bedroom). 800 sq ft is only the outer limit. For most houses the 50% rule gives a smaller number, so measure those rooms (143-6.2, in-law suite (1))",
      "One per lot. No outside change that makes the house or garage look like anything other than a single-family house or a garage (143-6.2, in-law suite (3))",
      "The owner signs a written agreement with the Township, recorded with the Recorder of Deeds, naming the occupants and describing the suite. A separate zoning permit (143-6.2, in-law suite (4), (5))",
      "One more off-street parking space than the house needs (143-6.2, in-law suite (14))",
      "No more than one detached household garage per lot (district use lists). No separate height or yard rule for a household garage was found. The district yards and building height apply",
      "R-3, R-4 and R-5 cap density at 3.0 dwelling units per gross acre for single-family, twin and duplex dwellings. Whether the in-law suite counts toward it is not settled. Ask the zoning officer"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Lower Providence Township (lowerprovidence.org). Read on eCode360 in a browser, one page at a time, the in-law suite text from screenshots of the Article I page. Use lists checked for R-1 to R-5, and code searches for 'in-law suite' and 'household garage'. District area and height rules read for R-1 to R-5. Off-street parking (143-71) was not opened."
